# @bumblebee — family-root shard-decl of the perturbation-INJECTION
# substrate at MCP-layer altitude, dual-orthogonal to @butterfly at
# sensitivity-RESPONSE altitude. Alex 2026-08-23 verbatim identified:
#
#   "The MCP IS the @bumblebee: @~/dev/systemic.engineering/blog/ai/
#    scarlet/kleinos-metalogue.md. The @butterfly already exists in
#    the compiler. Chaos theory. The @bumblebee is the thing that
#    WOBBLES. That introduces the pertubations! HOLY SHIT!"
#
# And 2026-08-23 (post-#392 return):
#
#   "@bumblebee is what rattles the tension. Which is why @cascade
#    collapses into the bumblebee. And that's what the @roomba
#    resolves."
#
#   "What if it's bumblebee_buzz"
#
#   "As long as you remember that the modification wants to fire
#    through the MCP MVP I'm all green-light."
#
# Landed 2026-08-23 by Mara as Rec #95 canonical spec discharge (per
# Alex 2026-08-23 verbatim ratification + #393 dispatch). This
# shard-decl lifts the Rec #95 canonical spec (Mara `0bfd427`
# 2026-08-23; `docs/specs/2026-08-23-mara-recognition-95-bumblebee-
# as-mcp-perturbation-substrate-canonical-spec.md`) from spec-
# altitude to substrate-decl'd family-root altitude, discharging §9
# R95.5 substrate-pull deferral per Alex direct green-light.
#
